  "prompt": "/deep-research According to table 2.2 in the ICILS 2023 international report, which countries had the most categories for both CIL and CT education which were \"Available but not compulsory to teach\" for ISCED 1 level education?",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "According to table 2.2 in the ICILS 2023 international report, which countries had the most categories for both CIL and CT education which were \"Available but not compulsory to teach\" for ISCED 1 level education?",
  "answer": "Based on Table 2.2 of the ICILS 2023 International Report (page 56), the countries with the **most categories** marked as \"Available but not compulsory to teach\" (◇) for **both** CIL and CT at ISCED 1 (primary) level are:\n\n**Netherlands** and **United States** — each with **4 out of 4 categories** for CIL and **4 out of 4 categories** for CT (the maximum possible, since there are 4 subject categories per domain at ISCED 1).\n\nOther notable countries with high counts in both domains:\n- **Oman**: 3 CIL, 4 CT\n- **Spain**: 2 CIL, 4 CT\n- **Serbia**: 2 CIL, 3 CT\n- **Austria**: 2 CIL, 3 CT\n\nThe table uses symbols: ◆ = Compulsory to teach, ◇ = Available but not compulsory to teach, − = Not taught. North Rhine-Westphalia (Germany) is a benchmarking participant, not a country.\n\n## Sources\n- https://www.iea.nl/sites/default/files/2024-11/ICILS_2023_International_Report_0.pdf",
  "answer_chars": 875,
  "expected_answer": "United States, Netherlands",
